{"author":"Unknown","author_email":"","data":{"content_hash":"33102ecfa2b8d2580a65ee265b45dc8dd074e49b59baf415526457793be54f06","digest":{"component_or_area":"code-review-tests LLM reviewer overlay and eval spec","key_entities":["src/rebar/llm/reviewers/code-review-tests.md","src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/code-review-tests.eval.yaml","src/rebar/llm/reviewers/index.json","src/rebar/llm/reviewers/criteria_routing.json","pytest.mark.skip","pytest.mark.xfail","strict=True","skipif","time.sleep"],"problem_keywords":["test sufficiency","code review rubric","non-gating tests","fault injection","false positives","antipatterns"],"propositions":["The code-review-tests rubric lacks named antipatterns for non-gating tests (unconditional or environment-dependent suppressions) and unrealistic fault injection (out-of-seam injection or sleep-only synchronization), causing missed test deficiencies at inference time.","New antipatterns must be added to the FLAG section of code-review-tests.md with explicit false-positive guards to avoid over-firing on strict xfails with stated reasons, environment-dependent skips in exercised CI contexts, and sleep used as secondary settling mechanism.","The eval spec must be extended with four new test cases (R-non-gating-skip, R-sleep-only-race, R-fault-wrong-seam, FP-strict-xfail-with-reason, FP-sleep-as-secondary) to validate recall and false-positive coverage without live inference.","The rubric addition must maintain existing front-matter, routing, threshold, and posture unchanged, with proof via regenerate-index consistency, git diff validation, and existing unit test suite passage."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1785825110228942068,"uuid":"ff35a4ae-8652-43a0-85ea-13692435aff5"}